      <h1 id="persistent-storage-using-iscsi" class="group scroll-mt-20">Persistent storage using iSCSI<a href="#persistent-storage-using-iscsi" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">You can provision your OpenShift Container Platform cluster with persistent storage by creating persistent volumes that pods can use to store and access data.</p>
      <p>Some familiarity with Kubernetes and iSCSI is assumed.</p>
      <p>The Kubernetes persistent volume framework allows administrators to provision a cluster with persistent storage and gives users a way to request those resources without having any knowledge of the underlying infrastructure.</p>
