      <h2 id="persistent-storage-iscsi-provisioning_persistent-storage-iscsi" class="group scroll-mt-20">Provisioning<a href="#persistent-storage-iscsi-provisioning_persistent-storage-iscsi" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can verify that the storage exists in the underlying infrastructure before mounting it as a volume in OpenShift Container Platform. All that is required for the iSCSI is the iSCSI target portal, a valid iSCSI Qualified Name (IQN), a valid LUN number, the filesystem type, and the <code>PersistentVolume</code> API.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the storage exists in the underlying infrastructure before mounting it as a volume in OpenShift Container Platform by creating the following <code>PersistentVolume</code> object definition:
